    "D": "$\\frac{5}{2}$\n\nOfficial Ans. by NTA (C)\nAns. (C)\nSol. $\\left|\\mathrm{z}_{2}+\\left|\\mathrm{z}_{2}-1\\right|\\right|^{2}=\\left|\\mathrm{z}_{2}-\\left|\\mathrm{z}_{2}+1\\right|\\right|^{2}$\n$$\\begin{array}{c}\n\\Rightarrow\\left|z_{2}+\\left|z_{2}-1\\right|\\right|\\left(\\bar{z}_{2}+\\left|z_{2}-1\\right|\\right)=\\left(z_{2}-\\left|z_{2}+1\\right|\\right)\\left(\\bar{z}_{2}-\\left(z_{2}+1\\right)\\right) \\\\\n\\Rightarrow \\quad z_{2}\\left|\\bar{z}_{2}+12_{2}-1\\right|-\\left(\\bar{z}_{2}-\\left|z_{2}+1\\right|\\right)+\\bar{z}_{2}\\left(\\left|z_{2}-1\\right|+\\left|z_{2}+1\\right|\\right) \\\\\n=\\left|z_{2}+1\\right|^{2}=\\left|z_{2}-1\\right|^{2} \\\\\n\\Rightarrow\\left[z_{2}+\\bar{z}_{2}\\right)\\left(\\left|z_{2}-1\\right|\\right)+\\left(z_{2}+1 \\mid\\right)=2\\left(z_{2}+\\bar{z}_{2}\\right) \\\\\n\\Rightarrow\\left(z_{2}+\\bar{z}_{2}\\right)\\left(\\left|z_{2}-1\\right|+\\left|z_{2}+1\\right|-2\\right)=0 \\\\\n\\therefore z_{2}+\\bar{z}_{2}=0 \\text { or }\\left|z_{2}-1\\right|+\\left|z_{2}+1\\right|-2=0\n\\end{array}$$\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{z}_{2}$ lie on imaginary axis. Or on real axis with in [-1,1]\n\nAlso $\\left|z_{1}-3\\right|=\\frac{1}{2}$ lie on circle having centre 3 and radius $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nClearly $\\left|z_{1}-z_{2}\\right| \\min =\\frac{5}{2}-1=\\frac{3}{2}$\n16. The foot of the perpendicular from a point on the circle $\\mathrm{x}^{2}+\\mathrm{y}^{2}=1, \\mathrm{z}=0$ to the plane $2 \\mathrm{x}+3 \\mathrm{y}+\\mathrm{z}=6$ lies on which one of the following curves ?\n(A) $(6 \\mathrm{x}+5 \\mathrm{y}-12)^{2}+4(3 \\mathrm{x}+7 \\mathrm{y}-8)^{2}=1$,\n$$z=6-2 x-3 y$$\n(B) $(5 \\mathrm{x}+6 \\mathrm{y}-12)^{2}+4(3 \\mathrm{x}+5 \\mathrm{y}-9)^{2}=1$,\n$$z=6-2 x-3 y$$\n(C) $(6 \\mathrm{x}+5 \\mathrm{y}-14)^{2}+9(3 \\mathrm{x}+5 \\mathrm{y}-7)^{2}=1$,\n$$z=6-2 x-3 y$$\n(D) $(5 \\mathrm{x}+6 \\mathrm{y}-14)^{2}+9(3 \\mathrm{x}+7 \\mathrm{y}-8)^{2}=1$,\n$$z=6-2 x-3 y$$\n\nOfficial Ans. by NTA (B)\nAns. (B)\nSol.\n$$\\begin{array}{l}\n\\frac{\\mathrm{h}-\\cos \\theta}{2}=\\frac{\\mathrm{k}-\\sin \\theta}{3}=\\frac{\\mathrm{w}-0}{1} \\\\\n=\\frac{-1(2 \\cos \\theta+3 \\sin \\theta-6)}{14} \\\\\n\\mathrm{~h}=\\cos \\frac{-2(2 \\cos \\theta+3 \\sin \\theta-6)}{14} \\\\\n=\\frac{10 \\cos \\theta-6 \\sin \\theta+12}{14} \\\\\n\\mathrm{k}=\\sin \\theta-\\frac{3}{14}(2 \\cos \\theta+3 \\sin \\theta-6) \\\\\n\\mathrm{k}=\\frac{5 \\sin \\theta-6 \\cos \\theta+18}{14}\n\\end{array}$$\n\nElementary $\\sin \\theta$ and $\\cos \\theta$\n$$(5 h+6 k-12)^{2}+4(3 h+5 k-9)^{2}=1$$\n\nJEE Exam Solution\nwww.esaral.com\n6"
